.066667 .066667 .066667 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 163.5 Tm /F1 10.5 Tf 14.5 TL -0.130743 Tw (Pakistan's RMB clearing infrastructure has been built in stages over roughly a decade. The State) Tj T* 0 Tw -0.027243 Tw (Bank of Pakistan first approved the Industrial and Commercial Bank of China \(ICBC\) to establish) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.100173 Tw (a local Yuan clearing and settlement mechanism in 2015, followed by Bank of China in 2018,) Tj T* 0 Tw .088967 Tw (and Standard Chartered Pakistan, the country's oldest foreign bank, was separately approved in) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.418342 Tw (March 2019 to open its own Yuan clearing and settlement setup \(thenews.com.pk\). The) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.640592 Tw (arrangement was formalised further in October 2023, when the People's Bank of China) Tj T* 0 Tw 4.17026 Tw (designated ICBC's Karachi branch as Pakistan's official RMB clearing bank, connecting) Tj T* 0 Tw .686757 Tw (Pakistan's offshore Yuan market directly to China's onshore market, on the same day a similar) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.434736 Tw (clearing bank was launched in Laos \(english.news.cn\). ICBC's Karachi branch had already) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.580007 Tw (become the first bank in South Asia admitted as a direct participant in China's Cross-Border) Tj T* 0 Tw .430257 Tw (Interbank Payment System, or CIPS, in 2020, and today offers RMB forwards, swaps, letters of) Tj T* 0 Tw (credit, guarantees, and structured trade financing directly out of Pakistan \(cgtn.com\).) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 74.0315 91.85039 cm
q
.066667 .066667 .066667 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 178 Tm /F1 10.5 Tf 14.5 TL 8.099789 Tw (The volume moving through this infrastructure has grown accordingly. Pakistan's) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.1771 Tw (Yuan-denominated imports from China rose from 5.6 per cent of the total in 2016 to 19.1 per) Tj T* 0 Tw -0.099963 Tw (cent in 2025, and have reportedly reached close to 25 per cent in 2026 \(chinapulse.com\). In May) Tj T* 0 Tw .146738 Tw (2026, Pakistan issued its first ever Panda Bond, a Yuan denominated sovereign instrument sold) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.009173 Tw (in China's own domestic bond market, raising RMB 1.75 billion, roughly USD 250 million, at a) Tj T* 0 Tw 4.523873 Tw (2.5 per cent coupon over a three year tenor; the offering was more than five times) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.465173 Tw (oversubscribed against total bids of RMB 8.8 billion, and sits within a wider USD 1 billion) Tj T* 0 Tw .493191 Tw (programme supported by the Asian Development Bank and the Asian Infrastructure Investment) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.763757 Tw (Bank \(dawn.com\). Behind this sits a bilateral currency swap line between the State Bank of) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.452725 Tw (Pakistan and the People's Bank of China that has stood at RMB 30 billion, roughly USD 4.2) Tj T* 0 Tw .46835 Tw (billion, since 2020 and was last renewed at that level in October 2024; in April 2025, Pakistan's) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.979315 Tw (Finance Minister formally requested that China raise the ceiling to RMB 40 billion, telling) Tj T* 0 Tw (reporters Islamabad had already exhausted the existing facility \(businesstoday.in\).) Tj T* ET
