BT 1 0 0 1 0 149 Tm /F1 10.5 Tf 14.5 TL 2.126392 Tw (Two practical steps follow. First, a Chinese firm evaluating Pakistan should ask its banking) Tj T* 0 Tw 5.218191 Tw (partner, whether ICBC, Bank of China, or Standard Chartered, precisely which RMB) Tj T* 0 Tw .48266 Tw (denominated financing products are actually available today, including trade credit, guarantees,) Tj T* 0 Tw 2.984342 Tw (and short term working capital lines, rather than assuming that clearing capability implies) Tj T* 0 Tw 3.562717 Tw (financing capability; the Carnegie findings on absent product lines suggest this gap has) Tj T* 0 Tw .398773 Tw (persisted for several years and should be tested directly rather than taken on faith. Second, the) Tj T* 0 Tw .713073 Tw (swap line drawdown pattern is itself a useful leading indicator worth monitoring: a renewal at a) Tj T* 0 Tw .216594 Tw (stable ceiling is routine, but a formal request to raise the ceiling, as Pakistan made in April 2025) Tj T* 0 Tw .1801 Tw (after exhausting the existing facility \(businesstoday.in\), signals system wide RMB liquidity stress) Tj T* 0 Tw .635757 Tw (rather than routine housekeeping, and is the kind of practical, ground level detail that deserves) Tj T* 0 Tw (closer and more continuous tracking than it currently receives.) Tj T* ET
